CORE broken-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--smt2 --add-triggers --outfile -
\(forall \(\(\|main::1::1::j[^|]*\| \(_ BitVec 32\)\)\) \(! .*:pattern \(\(select array\.[0-9]+ \(\(_ zero_extend 32\) \|main::1::1::j[^|]*\|\)\)\)\)\)
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Verify that `--add-triggers` causes the non-incremental SMT2 backend to wrap
the body of every quantifier with `(! BODY :pattern (...))`.  The trigger for
this harness is the array read `a[j]`, which becomes
`(select array.<n> ((_ zero_extend 32) |main::1::1::j...|))` in SMT-LIB.

The test only inspects the raw SMT2 output (using `--outfile -`); we tag it
with `broken-smt-backend` to keep it out of the per-solver test profiles, in
the same style as `array_of_bool_as_bitvec/test-smt2-outfile.desc`.
